WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.942
This is Coding Exercise 1.

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:07.147
Your task is to return patient ID, patient name, admission ID, diagnosis,

00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:11.217
and department for patients who have admissions.

00:00:11.217 --> 00:00:15.947
The phrase patients who have admissions tells you that a match is required.

00:00:15.947 --> 00:00:19.477
We are not trying to preserve patients with no admission.

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.712
That points toward INNER JOIN.

00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:26.007
Start with patients as one table and admissions as the related table.

00:00:26.007 --> 00:00:28.442
The relationship is patient ID.

00:00:28.442 --> 00:00:32.197
Select the requested columns and sort the result as instructed.

00:00:32.197 --> 00:00:35.562
Do not try to force one row per patient.

00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:39.632
The correct grain is one row per matching admission.

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:45.952
If a patient has multiple admissions, that patient's information should appear on multiple rows.

00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:51.092
Before using Run and Check, predict what should happen to a patient with no admission.

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:56.217
After running, compare the number of result rows with the number of matching admissions.

00:00:56.217 --> 00:01:01.432
If the checker does not pass, inspect the requested columns, join condition,

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:04.195
and grain before changing syntax randomly.
